---
title: Design class diagram 5 of 8 - API controllers, part 1 (Strategies.Api/Controllers)
---
classDiagram
    direction LR

    class AuthController {
        <<controller api/auth>>
        -_authService: IAuthService
        -_emailService: IEmailService
        -_configuration: IConfiguration
        +Login(request: LoginRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +Refresh(request: RevokeTokenRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +Revoke(request: RevokeTokenRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +ForgotPassword(request: ForgotPasswordRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +Register(request: RegisterRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +ResetPassword(request: ResetPasswordRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +Me() Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class LeadsController {
        <<controller api/leads>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetLeads(page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 10, search: string?, status: string?) Task~IActionResult~
        +CreateLead(dto: CreateLeadRequest, agentService: IAgentService) Task~IActionResult~
        +UpdateLeadStatus(id: Guid, request: UpdateLeadStatusRequest) Task~IActionResult~
    }
    class CasesController {
        <<controller api/cases>>
        -_context: ApplicationDbContext
        +GetCases(page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 10, search: string?, stage: string?) Task~IActionResult~
        +CreateCase(request: CreateCaseRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +GetCase(id: Guid) Task~IActionResult~
        +ExportCases() Task~IActionResult~
        +GetClientCases(clientId: Guid, page: int = 1, pageSize: int = 10) Task~IActionResult~
        +UpdateStage(id: Guid, request: UpdateCaseStageRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        +AssignConsultant(id: Guid, request: AssignConsultantRequest) Task~IActionResult~
        -EscapeCsv(value: string)$ string
    }

    class IAuthService {
        <<interface, see diagram 7>>
    }
    class IEmailService {
        <<interface, see diagram 8>>
    }
    class IAgentService {
        <<interface, see diagram 8>>
    }
    class ApplicationDbContext {
        <<DbContext, see diagram 8>>
    }

    AuthController --> IAuthService
    AuthController --> IEmailService
    LeadsController ..> IAgentService : «use» per request
    LeadsController --> ApplicationDbContext
    CasesController --> ApplicationDbContext

    note "All controllers extend ControllerBase; dependencies arrive by<br>constructor injection (the private fields). Optional string<br>parameters default to null. Access rules:<br>AuthController: anonymous, except Me (signed in). Login,<br>ForgotPassword, Register, ResetPassword: auth-strict rate limit.<br>LeadsController: CreateLead anonymous (agentService from<br>FromServices); GetLeads, UpdateLeadStatus Admin or Consultant.<br>CasesController: signed in. AssignConsultant Admin only;<br>GetCase, GetClientCases any role; the rest Admin or Consultant."
